AdaptedCoordinateStarData`, with no supplied\n  finite-stage `StarAlgEquiv` field;\n- `directedFamily`: the coherent finite-stage system;\n- `alpha`: the resulting algebraic direct-limit `StarAlgEquiv`;\n- `alpha_word`, `alpha_zWord`, `alpha_xWord`, `alpha_symm_word`, and\n  `existsUnique_alpha`: the phase-calibrated word and inverse formulas and\n  uniqueness; and\n- `standardAlphaData`: a tautological non-vacuity witness on `Nat`.\n\nThe conditional premises are explicit fields of `AlphaData`:\n\n1. P52's `LocalHyperbolicFamily.indep` and `LatticeExhaustion` data;\n2. `[LinearOrder I]`, used solely for the quadratic-phase ordering convention;\n3. `symplectic`, equality of the antisymmetrized source and target Pauli\n   pairings; and\n4. `stage_surjective`, onto-ness of each finite source-label block onto its\n   regional target-label block.\n\nP52 already proves injectivity and inclusion coherence. P53 derives stage\nbijectivity by combining that proof with `stage_surjective`; it does not hide\nstage equivalences, phase calibration, or whole-stage coherence in fields.\nThe local `symplectic` and `stage_surjective` conditions are additional\nauxiliary assumptions, not consequences established from the manuscript in\nthis repository.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | From the named P52 data plus `symplectic` and `stage_surjective`, P53 constructs the finite twisted Pauli algebras, phase-calibrated finite-stage star equivalences, commuting directed system, and algebraic direct-limit star equivalence `alpha`. |\n| partial | The manuscript specialization is conditional: the repository does not construct the actual regional symplectic-coordinate realization or prove the stage-surjectivity premise from the cited manuscript clauses. The formula on generators is phase-calibrated, not an unphased literal equality. |\n| blocked | No obstruction blocks this algebraic gate. The next gates—concrete C-star realization/extension, product-state identity, GNS spatial tensor splitting, factorhood, and trace/weight classification—remain P54--P59 work. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is met at its stated conditional scope. The\nalternative route builds a project-local finite twisted-word algebra rather\nthan assuming stage equivalences. This adds precisely `symplectic` and\n`stage_surjective` as premises; it does not weaken the requested conclusion.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P53, Lane H.\n- **Predecessors:** P52 is integrated, compiled, and locally audited in\n  `reviews/P52-coherent-local-hyperbolic-coordinates-closeout.md`. The module\n  imports P52 plus checked phase/coherence/direct-limit infrastructure; it\n  imports no later P54--P61 package.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged: constructed phase-calibrated finite-stage\n  star equivalences, their coherent algebraic direct-limit equivalence, and\n  the direct-limit `alpha` word formulas.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected. The module explicitly makes no\n  C-star completion, state identity, GNS tensor split, spatial tensor-product,\n  factorhood, trace, or weight theorem, and no such declaration occurs.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean` — passed\n  in the live project (8045 jobs); no build ran in quarantine.\n- `lake build` — passed in the live project.\n- `lake env lean /dev/stdin` with `#print axioms` for\n  `stageLabelMap_bijective`, `stage_mulCompatible`, `stage_starCompatible`,\n  `directedFamily`, `alpha`, `alpha_word`, `alpha_zWord`, `alpha_xWord`,\n  `existsUnique_alpha`, and `standardAlphaData` — each reports only\n  `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder scan across the candidate and its direct P52/phase/direct-limit\n  imports — no `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`,\n  `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` occurrence.\n- Quarantine/live SHA-256 comparison and `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding. The review checked that finite-stage\nsurjectivity is exposed rather than inferred from P52, that symmetry of the\ndiscrepancy is obtained only from the named symplectic premise, that the\nquadratic phase is used in both multiplication and star compatibility, and\nthat `alpha_zWord`/`alpha_xWord` retain the phase. Compilation validates the\nformal conditional construction; it does not establish the manuscript's\ngeometric realization or any later analytic/operator-algebraic statement.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P53 candidate, its response archive,\nquarantine extraction, and this review. Pre-existing untracked P49/P49A/P49B\ncandidate and review files remain untouched. No manuscript file was changed;\nno commit, push, dependency update, archive build, or dependency fetch was\nperformed.\n=== reviews/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge-closeout.md\n# P55A closeout review — local-hyperbolic finite-stage UHF bridge\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated infrastructure-only Lane-H scope; queue may\nadvance.**\n\nThe terminal status for Aristotle task\n`2e89017e-ccab-47c2-bd66-ca42164fd972` is `COMPLETE` in\n`history/logs/20260808T161409Z-1ac3c887-tasks.log`.\nIts exact archive\n`aristotle_responses/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge-1ac3c887-2e89017e.tar.gz`\nwas extracted only to\n`aristotle_responses/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge-1ac3c887-2e89017e-quarantine/`.\nNo build, update, or dependency fetch was run in that dependency-free\nsnapshot.  Only the packet-authorized candidate\n`AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicFiniteStageUHFBridge.lean` was\nintegrated into the live project.  Its live and quarantine SHA-256 values\nagree:\n\n```text\n42b18ef984b2046a4004ae64e8e79a0df7454e0c122b8d9722145bc6e2d28b3a\n```\n\nNo raw response record was integrated: the packet authorizes only the\ncandidate module.  The archive and quarantine extraction are retained as raw\nevidence.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nThe new module imports the accepted P53 module\n`AristotleCandidates.LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha` and\n`Formalization.DyadicTensorTower`; their archived versions are\nbyte-identical to the live versions.  It constructs, rather than receives as\na field:\n\n- `UHFBridge.qubitMatrixEquiv k :\n  QubitTensorPower k ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] Matrix (Reg (Fin k)) (Reg (Fin k)) ℂ`;\n- recursive dyadic words `qubitX`, `qubitZ`, and\n  `qubitWord k a b := qubitX k a * qubitZ k b`;\n- `AlphaData.sourceStageMatrixEquiv n e`, obtained from P53's\n  `pauliWordBasis`, the explicitly proved matrix-word basis\n  `stdWordBasis`, and the supplied enumeration\n  `e : A.Coord n ≃ Fin k`; and\n- the packet target\n\n  ```lean\n  A.sourceStageUHFEquiv n e :\n    pauliAlgebra (A.sourceForm n) ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] QubitTensorPower k\n  ```\n\n  defined by transport through the constructed register-matrix equivalence.\n\nThe exact word and generator formulae are:\n\n```lean\nA.sourceStageUHFEquiv n e (pauliWord (A.sourceForm n) v) =\n  qubitWord k (A.enumRepr n e v).1 (A.enumRepr n e v).2\n\nA.sourceStageUHFEquiv n e\n    (pauliWord (A.sourceForm n) ((A.stageCoordinates n).z i)) =\n  qubitZ k (Pi.single (e i) 1)\n\nA.sourceStageUHFEquiv n e\n    (pauliWord (A.sourceForm n) ((A.stageCoordinates n).x i)) =\n  qubitX k (Pi.single (e i) 1)\n```\n\nThey are exported as `sourceStageUHFEquiv_word`,\n`sourceStageUHFEquiv_zGenerator`, and\n`sourceStageUHFEquiv_xGenerator`, together with\n`sourceStageUHFEquiv_bijective`,\n`sourceStageUHFEquivDefault` at `Nat.card (A.Coord n)`, and\n`norm_sourceStageUHFEquiv`,\n`norm_sourceStageMatrixEquiv`, and\n`isometry_sourceStageMatrixEquiv`.\n\nThe convention check is explicit.  The ordered word is `X^a Z^b`; its\nmultiplication sign is `(-1)^(b dot a')`, its star sign is\n`(-1)^(a dot b)`, and\n`i^(a dot b) X^a Z^b` is proved self-adjoint.  Both coordinate-generator\nimages have trivial fourth-root phase because their respective exponent\npairings vanish.  The recursive tensor convention puts coordinate zero in the\nouter matrix factor through `regSuccEquiv`; no unproved permutation is used.\n\nThere are no new mathematical premises.  The bridge inherits exactly P53's\n`AlphaData` data: a P52 locally supported hyperbolic family and exhaustion,\nplus the explicitly named auxiliary fields `symplectic` and\n`stage_surjective`.  The finite coordinate enumeration is constructed with\n`Finite.equivFin`; classical choice is not a supplied hypothesis.  Since\n`QubitTensorPower k` has no native normed additive structure in the pinned\nAPI, the candidate defines `qubitOpNorm` through the proved register-matrix\nmodel and states the distance-form isometry in that matrix model.  This is an\nexplicit norm-control route, not a hidden C-star completion premise.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | From every explicit enumeration `e`, the finite P53 source Pauli algebra is star-isomorphic to the corresponding recursive `k`-qubit dyadic stage; the word, X/Z-generator, multiplication, star, bijectivity, and induced norm statements are proved. |\n| partial | This is infrastructure only.  It does not construct the manuscript's actual coordinate realization; it inherits P53's named `AlphaData` assumptions and does not identify any direct limit. |\n| blocked | None at the P55A gate. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is met exactly at its stated scope.  The\nsupporting matrix route is not a weakened target: it constructs an explicit\nstar equivalence between the recursive dyadic stage and its finite register\nmatrix model before transporting the explicitly constructed Pauli-word map.\nNo added premise or alternate conditional conclusion was introduced.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P55A, Lane H, as declared in the packet and the active\n  plan.\n- **Predecessors:** P53 only.  Its accepted,