nce, and that the custom dyadic norm is explicitly defined\nthrough the constructed matrix model.  It also checked the packet's scope\nagainst P55B--P59: no forbidden downstream statement is present.  Compilation\nand axiom reports validate this finite conditional infrastructure only; they\ndo not validate P53's external coordinate hypotheses or any manuscript\nregional-algebra conclusion.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P55A candidate, the exact archive and its\nquarantine extraction, and this closeout review.  The repository already had\nmodified plan/task/decision files and numerous untracked candidates, packets,\nand reviews; they were not overwritten, reformatted, or otherwise changed.\nNo manuscript file was modified; no commit, push, dependency update, archive\nbuild, or dependency fetch occurred.\n=== reviews/P55B-local-hyperbolic-source-uhf-bridge-closeout.md\n# P55B closeout review — local-hyperbolic source/UHF bridge\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated infrastructure-only Lane-H scope; queue may\nadvance.**\n\nAristotle task `5b40a5f6-d59a-4281-b6db-b103e3692cfd` is terminal\n`COMPLETE` in\n`history/logs/20260808T174500Z-809ad1ae-tasks.log`.\nIts exact response archive\n`aristotle_responses/P55B-local-hyperbolic-source-uhf-bridge-809ad1ae-5b40a5f6.tar.gz`\nwas extracted only into\n`aristotle_responses/P55B-local-hyperbolic-source-uhf-bridge-809ad1ae-5b40a5f6-quarantine/`.\nNo build, update, or dependency fetch was run in that dependency-free\nsnapshot. Only the packet-authorized module\n`AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicSourceUHFBridge.lean` was integrated into\nthe live project. Its live and quarantine SHA-256 values agree:\n\n```text\nf754604e0c6a1f870158f81cda06223a86364d0a461816b9e9e5e7c9f7261cad\n```\n\nThe archived P53 and P55A predecessor modules are byte-identical to their\nlocally integrated, audited counterparts (respectively\n`797dd652c0cef03fd6481aee5331446fdad4dba7f4db9f310bda6d6b76efcd1b`\nand\n`42b18ef984b2046a4004ae64e8e79a0df7454e0c122b8d9722145bc6e2d28b3a`).\nNo raw response record was integrated: the packet authorizes only this\ncandidate module; the archive and quarantine extraction remain raw evidence.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nThe module imports only the accepted P55A bridge and\n`Formalization.DyadicTensorTower`; through P55A it uses the accepted P53\nsource system. It adds no axiom, supplied coherent enumeration, supplied\ncommuting square, supplied cofinality, or supplied direct-limit equivalence.\nThe load-bearing declarations are:\n\n- `AlphaData.stageEnum`, `stageEnum_coherent`, and\n  `enumRepr_sourceIncl`: a constructed birth-stage/linear-order enumeration\n  of nested coordinate blocks, with old coordinates shifted exactly as the\n  dyadic embeddings require;\n- `stageUHFEquiv` and `stageUHFEquiv_sourceConnecting`: the P55A finite-stage\n  equivalences in those enumerations and their proved commuting square with\n  P53's `sourceConnecting`;\n- `CoordinateDyadicLimit`, `coordDyadicDirected`,\n  `sourceToCoordinateDyadic`, `sourceToCoordinateDyadic_of`, and\n  `sourceToCoordinateDyadic_unique`: the constructed coordinate dyadic limit,\n  the source-limit star equivalence, its canonical-stage formula, and\n  uniqueness from those formulas;\n- `stageCard_cofinal`, `coordinateDyadicUHFEquiv`, `sourceUHFEquiv`,\n  `sourceUHFEquiv_of`, and `sourceUHFEquiv_unique`: the infinite-coordinate\n  branch under `[Infinite I]`; and\n- `terminalStage`, `stageCard_eq_card`, `terminalDyadicEquiv`,\n  `sourceFiniteEquiv`, `sourceFiniteEquiv_of`, and\n  `sourceFiniteEquiv_unique`: the terminal finite-coordinate branch under\n  `[Finite I]`.\n\nThe module inherits precisely P53's explicit `AlphaData` premises: P52's\nlocally supported hyperbolic family and exhaustion, `[LinearOrder I]`, and\nthe auxiliary `symplectic` and `stage_surjective` fields. The new endpoint\nassumptions are explicit and disjoint: `[Infinite I]` for the cofinal-UHF\nequivalence, and `[Finite I]` for the terminal-stage finite equivalence.\nThey are not claims derived from the manuscript. P55B introduces no new\nmathematical premise beyond these branch typeclasses and does not weaken the\npacket target.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | The coherent enumeration and the P55A/P53 commuting squares are constructed. They induce `sourceToCoordinateDyadic`. Under `[Infinite I]`, cofinal cardinalities give `sourceUHFEquiv : A.SourceLimit ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] QubitUHFAlgebra`; under `[Finite I]`, a terminal block gives `sourceFiniteEquiv : A.SourceLimit ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] QubitTensorPower (Nat.card I)`. The required canonical-stage formulas and uniqueness theorems are also proved. |\n| partial | This is infrastructure only. The result remains conditional on P53's named local-coordinate, symplecticity, and stage-surjectivity data. It neither constructs the manuscript's regional realization nor any analytic completion. |\n| blocked | None at the P55B gate. P55C's faithful concrete representations, P55D's C-star extension, and all P56--P59 state/GNS/factor/trace work remain downstream. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is met exactly at its stated conditional\nscope. The direct-limit route is an allowed project-local supporting theory:\nit changes no target and exposes every extra premise named above.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P55B, Lane H, as declared in the packet and `PLAN.md`.\n- **Predecessors:** only P53 and P55A. Both are locally integrated, compiled,\n  and semantically audited in\n  `reviews/P53-local-hyperbolic-algebraic-alpha-closeout.md` and\n  `reviews/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge-closeout.md`; the\n  archive proves they exactly match the live modules. No later P55C--P59\n  artifact is imported or used.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged: constructed finite-stage coherence, the\n  source-to-coordinate-dyadic direct-limit equivalence, and separate\n  finite-terminal/infinite-cofinal endpoint equivalences.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected. The candidate does not construct\n  an operator-range or C-star completion, a regional C-star alpha, a state\n  identity, GNS tensor splitting, factor classification, or trace/weight.\n  Its only occurrences of those topics are negative scope statements in the\n  module documentation.\n\nNo manuscript clause is represented by this infrastructure-only packet. In\nparticular, it does not promote the still-unformalized short-range regional\nvon Neumann-algebra theorem.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.LocalHyperbolicSourceUHFBridge` — passed in\n  the live project (`8051/8051` jobs). No build ran in quarantine.\n- `lake build` — passed in the live project (already up to date, `0` jobs).\n- `lake env lean /dev/stdin` importing the candidate and printing axioms for\n  `stageEnum_coherent`, `enumRepr_sourceIncl`,\n  `stageUHFEquiv_sourceConnecting`, `sourceToCoordinateDyadic`,\n  `sourceToCoordinateDyadic_unique`, `stageCard_cofinal`,\n  `coordinateDyadicUHFEquiv`, `sourceUHFEquiv`,\n  `sourceUHFEquiv_unique`, `sourceFiniteEquiv`, and\n  `sourceFiniteEquiv_unique` — each reports only `propext`,\n  `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder/declaration scan across the candidate and direct P53/P55A/dyadic\n  imports — no `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`,\n  `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` occurrence.\n- Quarantine/live SHA-256 comparison and `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding. The review checked that the enumeration\norders coordinates by birth stage and pads old registers in the direction used\nby the dyadic connecting maps; that the coherence square is extended from\nPauli-word basis elements rather than assumed; that cofinality uses the\nexplicit `[Infinite I]` branch; and that the finite result reaches a terminal\ncoordinate block only under `[Finite I]`. It further checked that no\none-directional direct-limit property was used as an equivalence without the\ntwo inverse maps, and that no forbidden Lane-H conclusion leaked into code.\nCompilation and axiom reports validate this conditional algebraic\ninfrastructure; they do not establish P53's external coordinate hypotheses,\nany C-star completion, or any manuscript/operator-algebraic conclusion.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P55B candidate, its exact response\narchive, quarantine extraction, and this closeout review. The pre-existing\nmodified plan/task/decision files and unrelated untracked candidates, packets,\nand reviews were preserved. No manuscript file was modified; no commit, push,\ndependency update, archive build, or dependency fetch occurred.\n=== reviews/P58-mixed-uhf-hyperfinite-factor-closeout.md\n# P58 closeout review — mixed UHF factor classification\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated mixed-sector, conditional Lane-H scope; queue may\nadvance.**\n\nAristotle task `ed55ef94-0313-4123-9cc0-b00ffdb465aa` was downloaded as\n`aristotle_responses/P58-mixed-uhf-hyperfinite-factor.tar.gz` (SHA-256\n`6a9c6e453986cbacfed106b03db592f946fd61c13acb976a9b9da8f4c3c7c7b5`) and\nextracted without building, updating, or fetching dependencies at\n`aristotle_responses/P58-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p58-3px4hkyb_aristotle/`.\nOnly the packet-authorized module\n`AristotleCandidates/MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean` was integrated into the\nlive project. Its quarantine and live SHA-256 values agree:\n`5dbf9ff8c35035c94b37804435793102cb0c59f88c7a39e2746c32274fc67d20`.\nThe archive and extraction remain raw response records. No manuscript file was\nchanged.\n\n## Source and exact declarations\n\nThe source basis is the narrow claim in `main.tex:1945-1967`, specifically the\nfinite maximally-mixed matrix alternative and the infinite maximally-mixed\nhyperfinite-II1 assertion at lines 1964-1966. This packet formalizes only the\nproject-local dyadic mixed sector; it neither establishes the preceding GNS\ntensor splitting nor transports its result to the manuscript's regional algebra.\n\nThe new module's load-bearing declarations are:\n\n- `qubitMatrixStarEquiv` (line 197) and\n  `qubitTensorTrace_eq_normalizedTrace` (line 213), identifying the `n`-qubit\n  algebra with `M_(2^n)(C)` and its trace with normalized matrix trace;\n- `qubitTensorPower_isMixedMatrixFactor` (line 291), whose explicit fields are\n  the star equivalence, positivity of `2^n`, normalized-trace identity,\n  traciality, faithfulness, and algebraic scalar centre;\n- `qubitUHF_hasScalarCenter` (line 314) and\n  `qubitUHF_not_matrixAlgebra` (line 331), the algebraic infinite-limit\n  statements;\n- `uhfConcreteCStar_isMatricialChain` (line 410), an increasing dense chain of\n  finite matrix subalgebras in the P54 concrete C-star model;\n- `matrixRange_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter` (line 683) and\n  `mixedStage_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter` (line 725), direct\n  matrix-unit proofs of trivial centre for each finite-stage generated concrete\n  von Neumann algebra;\n- `mixedVonNeumann` (line 739), defined as the von Neumann algebra generated\n  by `UHFConcreteCStar`; and\n- the conditional `mixedVonNeumann_isHyperfiniteFiniteFactor` (line 840).\n\nThe last theorem uses exactly the three fields of\n`MixedWeakClosurePremises` (lines 798-811): traciality of `uhfVectorState` on\nthe weak closure, faithfulness there, and `HasTrivialOperatorCenter` of that\nweak closure. `IsHyperfiniteFiniteFactorModel` (line 814) is explicitly a\nproject-local feature predicate: factorhood, a vector-normal faithful tracial\nstate, a matricial chain, and unbounded matrix sizes. It is **not** a proof of\nthe Murray-von Neumann/Connes uniqueness/classification theorem for the\nhyperfinite II1 factor.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | The finite mixed stage is star-isomorphic to `M_(2^n)(C)` with normalized faithful tracial functional and scalar centre. The algebraic UHF limit has scalar centre and is not a finite matrix algebra. In the P54 representation, finite matrix stages form a monotone dense C-star-level chain; each individual stage's generated von Neumann algebra has trivial centre by the local matrix-unit proof. The conditional theorem assembles the stated project-local finite-factor model. |\n| partial | Infinite weak-closure traciality, faithfulness, and factorhood are not proved; they are the three named fields above. The module's `IsVectorNormal` is a project-local single-vector-functional predicate, not a formalized Mathlib sigma-weak continuity theory. No canonical hyperfinite-II1 classification/isomorphism is formalized. |\n| blocked | Nothing blocks P58's stated gate, because the packet expressly permits an analytic factoriality/classification bridge only as an explicit conditional interface. Those analytic premises remain open for any later use. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is met at its stated scope. The alternate\nroute is a direct finite-matrix/matrix-unit construction plus a C-star-level\nmatricial approximation, rather than an unproved weak-closure transfer. It\nadds exactly the three `MixedWeakClosurePremises`; it does not silently weaken\nthe finite result or promote the conditional infinite result to a theorem of\nthe manuscript.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P58, Lane H — correct.\n- **Predecessors:** P54 is integrated, compiled, and audited in\n  `reviews/P54-uhf-reference-representation-closeout.md`. The imports\n  `Formalization.DyadicTensorTower`, P54's\n  `UHFReferenceRepresentation`, and the pre-existing local bicommutant core\n  are byte-identical between the quarantine snapshot and live checkout. The\n  bicommutant core is supporting infrastructure, not an undeclared later Lane-H\n  package dependency.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged: the finite mixed matrix alternative is\n  proved, and the infinite alternative supplies a checked matrix approximation\n  with all weak-closure/factor/classification gaps isolated as named premises.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected. The candidate contains no\n  regional alpha transport, pure-sector classification, spatial product\n  factorhood, regional factor claim, or final trace/weight theorem. Its\n  finite-stage factor statements and conditional mixed weak-closure model are\n  confined to the P54 dyadic reference representation.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor` — passed (8038\n  jobs) in the live project.\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.UHFReferenceRepresentation AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore AristotleCandidates.MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor Formalization` — passed (8089 jobs) in the live project.\n- `lake build` — passed in the live project; no work was required after the\n  focused build.\n- `lake env lean -o .lake/build/lib/lean/AristotleCandidates/MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.olean AristotleCandidates/MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean` — passed in the live project, producing the importable cache used by the axiom check.\n- `#print axioms` for `qubitTensorPower_isMixedMatrixFactor`,\n  `qubitUHF_hasScalarCenter`, `qubitUHF_not_matrixAlgebra`,\n  `uhfConcreteCStar_isMatricialChain`,\n  `matrixRange_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter`,\n  `mixedStage_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter`,\n  `uhfVectorState_isVectorNormal`, and\n  `mixedVonNeumann_isHyperfiniteFiniteFactor` — each reports only\n  `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Forbidden-declaration scan of the candidate and its three direct imports —\n  no `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`,\n  `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` occurrence.\n- Direct-import SHA-256 comparisons, candidate quarantine/live SHA-256\n  comparison, and `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding. The review checked the finite normalization\nagainst the actual recursive matrix equivalence; that the algebraic scalar-\ncentre proof first reduces an arbitrary limit element to a finite stage; that\nthe non-matrix result uses a finite-rank obstruction rather than a mere label;\nand that the matrix-unit proof establishes only trivial centre for each finite\ngenerated algebra. It also checked that `mixedVonNeumann` factorhood,\nfaithfulness, and traciality remain three separate explicit premises, and that\nthe project-local `IsHyperfiniteFiniteFactorModel` is not reported as a\nhyperfinite-II1 uniqueness theorem. Lean builds and axiom reports validate the\nformal statements, not the manuscript's unformalized GNS tensor splitting or\nthe open analytic closure bridge.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the P58 candidate, this closeout review, its raw archive,\nquarantine extraction, and the generated `.olean` under the existing\n`.lake/build/` cache. All previously untracked P49/P49A/P49B/P53 candidates\nand reviews remain untouched. No commit, push, dependency update, archive\nbuild, fetch, or manuscript modification was performed.\n=== work/FORMALIZATION-AUDIT-DECISION.md\n# Formalization semantic-audit decision\n\nDate: 2026-08-07\n\nThe approved deliverable is a semantic audit/tutorial of the Lean\nformalization, rather than another proof package or a compilation report.\n\nThe audit will provide:\n\n1. a status summary separating proved mathematics, conditional interfaces,\n   supplied data, and unformalized claims;\n2. a dependency map from the manuscript's finite-coordinate argument through\n   the algebraic limit, concrete C-star model, GNS transport, bicommutant\n   transport, and product-factor boundary;\n3. a theorem ledger mapping each important natural-language proof sentence to\n   exact Lean declarations, hypotheses, intermediate lemmas, and semantic\n   verdicts; and\n4. a step-by-step Lean reading sequence with code excerpts and direct build or\n   `#check` commands.\n\nThe audit must keep compilation separate from mathematical validity and must\nidentify exact manuscript locators from `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`. In particular,\nit must not call the regional hyperfinite-factor theorem proved merely because\nconditional Lean interfaces compile.\n\nThe first pass will inventory the current modules and completed-package\nreviews. Later passes will inspect the principal declarations and their proof\nchains in dependency order.\n=== work/FORMALIZATION-SEMANTIC-AUDIT.md\n# Formalization semantic audit\n\nStatus: first inventory in progress.\n\nThis document is the approved semantic/tutorial audit described in\n`FORMALIZATION-AUDIT-DECISION.md`. It is not itself a proof and does not\nchange the manuscript theorem status.\n\n## Audit verdict convention\n\n- **proved**: the stated Lean theorem follows from its explicit hypotheses and\n  compiles without placeholders;\n- **conditional**: the Lean implication is proved, but one or more hypotheses\n  are supplied structures or external analytic assumptions;\n- **infrastructure**: reusable Lean mathematics with no manuscript claim;\n- **unformalized**: a manuscript step for which no corresponding theorem is\n  currently present;\n- **not aligned**: the Lean conclusion is stronger, weaker, or materially\n  different from the natural-language sentence.\n\nCompilation, axiom reports, and mathematical alignment will be recorded\nseparately.\n\n## Source clauses\n\nThe manuscript-facing audit uses only the locators recorded in\n`SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`:\n\n- `main.tex:1671-1679`: local symplectic basis and finite-support condition;\n- `main.tex:1740-1752`: regional factor theorem statement;\n- `main.tex:1915-1920`: proposed adapted-basis star-isomorphism;\n- `main.tex:1927-1931`: pure/mixed product density state;\n- `main.tex:1945-1967`: GNS, tensor, and factor claims;\n- `main.tex:1970-2004`: quasi-equivalence and normal-folium claims.\n\n## Initial module inventory\n\nThe detailed theorem ledger and dependency graph are the next sections to be\nfilled after inspecting the principal declarations. The current theorem\ncontract itself still says:\n\n```lean\ndef regionalAlgebraTheoremStatus : String :=\n  \"conditional contract pending analytic model\"\n```\n\nThat status is consistent with the source contract and is not to be upgraded\nwithout discharging the missing finite-coordinate, representation, normality,\nand product-classification premises.\n\n## First-pass verdict\n\nThe current formalization is a sequence of conditional bridges, not yet a\nformal proof of the manuscript's regional factor theorem. The strongest\ncurrently checked route is:\n\n```text\nfinite adapted-coordinate data\n  -> finite StarAlgEquiv at each stage\n  -> coherent algebraic direct-limit StarAlgEquiv alpha\n  -> compatible algebraic state transport\n  -> supplied compatible operator representation\n  -> closed operator-range C*-algebra\n  -> supplied state-preserving C*-extension\n  -> GNS unitary and algebraic bicommutant transport\n  -> conditional product-factor/type classification\n```\n\nThe arrows are not all existence theorems. In particular, the source-specific\nfinite coordinate realization, a faithful representation of the algebraic\nlimit, the regional C*-extension, the analytic normality/WOT statements, and\nthe product-factor classification remain explicit premises or missing\nmathematics.\n\n## Status table for the reviewed overnight packages\n\n| Package | Principal Lean object | Semantic verdict | Main external premise |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P37 | `algebraicLimitOperatorRep` | conditional theorem proved | compatible finite-stage operator representations |\n| P38 | `quasilocalCStarAlgebra` | conditional theorem proved | supplied compatible representation; stage injectivity for faithfulness |\n| P39 | `StatePreservingData`, `gnsUnitary` | conditional theorem proved | C*-completion, alpha extension, state identity and continuity |\n| P40 | `bicommutantStarEquiv`, folium transport | algebraic part proved; analytic part conditional | WOT/double-commutant and normal-functional characterizations |\n| P41 | `ProductGNSFactorization` | partial boundary only | supplied factorization/classification; infinite weight interface is incomplete |\n| P42--P46 | no reviewed candidate currently present | not yet audited | candidate/archive status must be established before use |\n\nAll five reviewed packages compile in the local project. Their closeout\nreviews explicitly separate compilation from mathematical scope. P41 is\naccepted only as partial: its infinite-pure `TracialWeightCore` does not yet\nassert positivity, normality, faithfulness, or semifiniteness.\n\n## Dependency spine and one-to-one theorem anchors\n\n### 1. Finite coordinate map\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Given finite adapted source and target word bases, send each source word to a\n> phase-corrected target word.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nFiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData.starEquiv\nFiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData.starEquiv_word\nFiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData.starEquiv_correctedWord\n```\n\nSemantic status: the construction is proved from the fields of\n`FiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData`, but the actual manuscript-specific finite\ndata are not constructed from `main.tex:1671-1679` or `main.tex:1915-1920`.\n\n### 2. Coherence of finite maps\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> The finite coordinate maps commute with the inclusions of stages.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nstarEquiv_connecting_of_pauliBasis\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.stageEquiv_connecting\n```\n\nSemantic status: proved when word, label, phase, and connecting-map\ncompatibility are supplied.\n\n### 3. Algebraic infinite map\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Compatible finite maps descend to a unique star-isomorphism of algebraic\n> direct limits.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.alpha\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.alpha_of\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.existsUnique_alpha\n```\n\nSemantic status: this is a genuine algebraic direct-limit theorem, conditional\non the finite coherent family. It is not yet a C*-completion theorem.\n\n### 4. State transport\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Pull the target product state back along the algebraic alpha.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nTargetStageStates.targetLimitState\nTargetStageStates.pulledBackState\nTargetStageStates.pulledBackState_eq_targetLimitState_alpha\nTargetStageStates.pulledBackState_isAlgebraicState\n```\n\nSemantic status: the state-level implication is proved from compatible target\nstage states. The infinite product density operator itself is not constructed\nas a von Neumann-algebraic state in this module.\n\n### 5. Algebraic operator representation\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Compatible finite-stage operator representations define a representation of\n> the quasi-local algebra.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep_of\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep_stage_congr\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep_injective\n```\n\nSemantic status: proved conditionally. Injectivity requires stagewise\ninjectivity; no infinite tensor-product Hilbert space is constructed.\n\n### 6. Concrete C*-model\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Complete the quasi-local algebra in the operator norm.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nOperatorRepresentation.rangeClosure\nOperatorRepresentation.embedding\nOperatorRepresentation.denseRange_embedding\n```\n\nand, for the direct-limit range,\n\n```lean\nquasilocalCStarAlgebra\nquasilocalEmbedding\ndenseRange_quasilocalEmbedding\n```\n\nSemantic status: the closure is genuinely constructed inside bounded\noperators, but only after an isometric operator representation is supplied.\nThis does not prove that the manuscript's algebra has such a representation.\n\n### 7. State-preserving GNS transport\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> A state-preserving C*-isomorphism induces a canonical GNS unitary.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nStatePreservingData.sourceState_eq_pullback\nStatePreservingData.gnsUnitary\nStatePreservingData.gnsUnitary_intertwines\nStatePreservingData.gnsConjStarAlgEquiv\n```\n\nSemantic status: proved from supplied C*-completions, state positivity/order\ndata, continuity, and an exact state identity. It is not a proof of the\nmanuscript's state identity.\n\n### 8. Bicommutant transport\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> The GNS unitary identifies the represented von Neumann algebras.\n\nLean anchors:\n\n```lean\nStarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated\nStarSubalgebra.le_vonNeumannGenerated\nStarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated_le\nbicommutantStarEquiv_sourceRepVN\n```\n\nSemantic status: the algebraic bicommutant/conjugation statement is proved.\nThe identification with strong/weak operator closure and the normal-folium\nstep are conditional interfaces, not proved analytic theorems.\n\n### 9. Product-factor and trace conclusion\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> The product GNS algebra is a type-I pure factor tensor a finite type-I or\n> hyperfinite type-II1 mixed factor, with the appropriate trace conclusion.\n\nLean anchors:\n\n```lean cddddddddssssssssssssssssssssssssssw1\nProductGNSFactorization.pureFactor_typeI_of_finite\nProductGNSFactorization.pureFactor_typeIInfinity_of_infinite\nProductGNSFactorization.mixedFactor_typeI_of_finite\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
